Package: nmrpick
Type: Package
Title: Baseline Correction and Peak Detection for 1D NMR Metabolomics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Shrinidhi", "Bhat", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "shrinidhibhat59@gmail.com"),
    person("Satyam", role = "aut"),
    person("Senthamizh", "R", role = "aut"),
    person("Subhendu Kumar", "Nayak", role = "aut"),
    person("Sanjukta", "Patra", role = "aut"))
Description: Baseline correction (airPLS and a lighter binned-percentile
    alternative), dual-algorithm peak detection (shape/prominence-based
    and second-derivative), optional Lorentzian lineshape refinement,
    cross-sample peak alignment, and the per-compound group-comparison
    statistics (fold-change, Welch's t-test, exact Wilcoxon rank-sum
    test, Benjamini-Hochberg correction) used by this project's 1D 1H
    NMR metabolomics pipeline. Companion package to 'nmrmatch', which
    handles reference-library matching and confidence scoring. No
    Bioconductor dependency is required for the core functions; a direct
    Bruker 1D reader is included as an alternative to ASICS's own
    importSpectraBruker() for users who do not already have ASICS
    installed.
